@startuml storage-layer
' Jobinzy — storage layer (component diagram)
' Source of truth: src/lib/storage.ts

title Storage Layer — typed chrome.storage.local (Phase 1)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F0F7FF
  BorderColor #1A73E8
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #FFF4E0
  BorderColor #B26A00
}

package "storage.ts" {
  component "STORAGE_KEYS\njobinzy.profile / .answerBank /\n.aiSettings / .meta" as keys
  component "Profile: getProfile() · setProfile() · validateProfile()" as profile
  component "Answer bank: getAnswerBank() · upsertAnswerBankEntry() · deleteAnswerBankEntry()" as bank
  component "AI settings: getAISettings() · setAISettings() · DEFAULT_AI_SETTINGS" as aisettings
  component "Meta: getMeta() · setMeta() · DEFAULT_META" as meta
  component "runMigrations() — idempotent (1.2)" as migrate
  component "clearAllData() — destructive wipe (12.5)" as clear
  component "ValidationError" as err
}

database "chrome.storage.local" as store

profile --> store : read/write
bank --> store : read/write
aisettings --> store : read/write
meta --> store : read/write
clear --> store : remove profile/bank/aiSettings,\nreset meta.onboardingComplete=false
migrate --> meta : compares schemaVersion to\nCURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION (v1)

profile ..> err : throws if fullName/email/phone missing
bank ..> err : throws if questionText/answer empty
aisettings ..> err : throws if baseUrl/model empty

note bottom of store
  Error-handling contract (documented for every caller):
  • Getters (getProfile / getAnswerBank / getAISettings)
    return null or [] for missing data — never throw.
  • Setters THROW (ValidationError) on invalid input or
    storage failure — callers treat rejection as fatal
    for that write and surface it in the UI.
  No other module in src/ may call chrome.storage.local.*
  directly (AGENT.md §3 — grep-checked).
end note

note right of clear
  Keeps ExtensionMeta.schemaVersion,
  resets onboardingComplete → false so
  the next open shows onboarding again.
end note

@enduml
